   "style": "standard",
   "visual": null,
   "evidence": null,
   "points": [
    {
     "point_id": "pt_u1l1_5",
     "sentence": {
      "sentence_id": "sen_u1l1_07",
      "spans": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Qur’an describes this submission as a person’s prayer and worship — indeed their life and death — being for God, the Lord of all the worlds."
       }
      ],
      "source_ids": [
       "src_q_6_162_163"
      ]
     },
     "visual_params": null
    },
    {
     "point_id": "pt_u1l1_6",
     "sentence": {
      "sentence_id": "sen_u1l1_08",
      "spans": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Qur’an pairs submitting oneself to God with doing good; so Islam is not just a word that is said."
       }
      ],
      "source_ids": [
       "src_q_2_112"
      ]
     },
     "visual_params": null
    },
    {
     "point_id": "pt_u1l1_7",
     "sentence": {
      "sentence_id": "sen_u1l1_09",
      "spans": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Qur’an links Islam with trusting God, relying on Him in one’s heart."
       }
      ],
      "source_ids": [
       "src_q_10_84"
      ]
     },
     "visual_params": null
    },
    {
     "point_id": "pt_u1l1_8",
     "sentence": {
      "sentence_id": "sen_u1l1_10",
      "spans": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "So for Muslims, Islam is a relationship in which the whole person turns to God: worshipping Him alone, obeying Him, trusting Him and following His guidance."
       }
      ],
      "source_ids": [
       "src_tafsir_islam_meaning",
       "src_q_10_84"
      ]
